Today's class is a deliberate step back.

The findings from our student survey were clear: You want to spend more time on JavaScript fundamentals, the basics we blew by in our early weeks. And then, once you feel more comfortable, drill down on how you can use the language to load data and craft interactive pages.

So that's the plan.

Starting from a blank page, you'll build a new interactive page, step by step, with a focus on understanding the JavaScript concepts at work.

Once you're finished, you'll be ready to start building real data projects in our class's next phase.

## Part 1: Loading data, learning JavaScript

The data you're using is [film and television shoot permits](https://data.cityofnewyork.us/City-Government/Film-Permits/tg4x-b46p) published by New York City's Mayor's Office of Media and Entertainment. Every time a production company wants to prevent parking, block a sidewalk or take over a piece of city property, they file a permit. After a few months go by, those notices end up here.

